Subject: [PATCH 16/49] GDN chunked record: three-term bf16 state split; bench
 checks against an FP64 reference

s0.k and s0.q now see the full 24-bit state mantissa (hi on one accumulator, mid + lo on another).
Against FP64 (27B geometry, width 16) both kernels have rel.err 1.65e-3 (bf16 output rounding);
outputs that are not the correctly rounded value: staged 10, chunked 24 (was 53) of 98304 (tree).
